# Secrets — never committed, never read by AI agents (use .env.example instead)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Go (server/)
server/bin/
server/dist/
*.exe
# `go build ./cmd/<name>` with no -o drops the binary in the working directory, which for
# the server workspace is beside go.mod. Named rather than globbed: a bare `server/*`
# would hide a new package, and these three are the module's whole command list.
server/voxelheimd
server/voxelheim-auth
server/voxelheim-voicebot

# A server run with the default -world-dir writes its saved chunks here. Deltas only —
# the generated terrain is a function of the seed — but it is local state, not source.
# The versioned forms require a digit after `world-v`. The later exceptions put back any
# name containing a non-digit suffix, so `world-vendor` and `world-v1-notes` remain visible.
/world/
server/world/
/world-v[0-9]*/
server/world-v[0-9]*/
!/world-v*[!0-9]*/
!/world-v*[!0-9]/**
!server/world-v*[!0-9]*/
!server/world-v*[!0-9]/**

# The account service keeps its Ed25519 signing key under -auth-dir, whose default is
# `auth` — resolved against the working directory, so running it from server/ puts a
# **private key** inside this repository. Ignored by directory for the default and for
# the name the README suggests, and then by file name anywhere, because -auth-dir takes
# whatever an operator types and the second rule is the one that still holds when they
# type something else.
#
# The file-name rules are not redundant with the directory ones, and the reason is worth
# knowing: `scripts/check-publication-privacy.sh` scans with `git grep -I`, which skips
# binary files — so a committed key would pass every check this repository runs. Nothing
# downstream would catch it, which is why it is caught here.
/auth/
server/auth/
/authdata/
server/authdata/
signing-key.bin
verifying-key.bin

# The TLS identity, by file name for the reason the two above are: both services keep one
# — the game server under -world-dir, the account service under -auth-dir (#131) — and
# both flags take whatever an operator types. `server-key.pem` is a **private key**, and
# the directory rules only cover the paths this repository suggests.
server-cert.pem
server-key.pem

# Rust (client/)
client/target/
target/

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Logs and scratch
*.log

# Graphify output (graphify-out/): every analysis artifact is generated and local-only —
# graph.json, graph.html, GRAPH_REPORT.md and the runtime environment (.graphify_python).
graphify-out/

# Python bytecode (test runs)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
